/// newspeak-spec.pdf 6.2: the result of a mixin application "is a class I
/// with mixin M and superclass S", and its instance initializer runs S's
/// initializer and then M's "on o with the arguments of mu_m". Nothing
/// there forbids applying one mixin twice in one chain.
///
/// Twice is Base withBase: 'b' <: Marker tag: 'lower' <: Middle
/// <: Marker tag: 'upper': four levels over Base, Marker's mixin at the
/// first and the third. So:
///
/// - Each Marker level is its own application with its own subobject, so
///   Marker's initializer runs twice, once per clause, each with its own
///   clause's argument, in the chain's order (the first four lines).
/// - Adding a second Marker level must leave every other level's slots
///   where they were: Base's two slots, Middle's and Twice's own each read
///   back what their initializers stored.
/// - who is declared by Marker, Middle and Base; the upper Marker level is
///   the nearest to Twice, so it answers. Its markerTag is a protected slot
///   read, an implicit receiver send that 5.7 turns into outer Marker
///   markerTag, which at k = 0 is looked up on the receiver's class (5.9's
///   lookupProtected): the upper level's getter, answering 'upper'.
/// - chain climbs by super from the upper Marker level through Middle and
///   the lower Marker level to Base (5.10), one step per level.
/// - belowSees is Middle's super markerSees, which runs the lower Marker
///   level's method; its markerTag is the same virtual send, so it too
///   answers the upper level's 'upper': the topmost application wins a
///   selector even when the lower one's own method sends it.
class MixinSameMixinAppliedTwiceInOneChain = Object new (| t ::= nil. |) (
    class Base withBase: value = Object new (|
        baseFirst = outer MixinSameMixinAppliedTwiceInOneChain note: 'Base' receives: value, '1'.
        baseSecond = value, '2'.
    |) (
        public who = ( ^'Base' )
        public chain = ( ^'Base' )
        public baseSlots = ( ^baseFirst, ' ', baseSecond )
    ) : ()
    class Marker tag: value = Object new (|
        markerTag = outer MixinSameMixinAppliedTwiceInOneChain note: 'Marker' receives: value.
    |) (
        public who = ( ^'Marker tagged ', markerTag )
        public chain = ( ^'Marker > ', super chain )
        public markerSees = ( ^markerTag )
    ) : ()
    class Middle = Object new (|
        middleSlot = outer MixinSameMixinAppliedTwiceInOneChain note: 'Middle' receives: 'm'.
    |) (
        public who = ( ^'Middle' )
        public chain = ( ^'Middle > ', super chain )
        public middleSlotValue = ( ^middleSlot )
        public belowSees = ( ^super markerSees )
    ) : ()
    class Twice = Base withBase: 'b' <: Marker tag: 'lower' <: Middle <: Marker tag: 'upper' (|
        twiceSlot = outer MixinSameMixinAppliedTwiceInOneChain note: 'Twice' receives: 't'.
    |) (
        public twiceSlotValue = ( ^twiceSlot )
    ) : ()
    public note: name receives: value = (
        t show: name, ' initializer receives ', value; newLine.
        ^value
    )
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        | twice |
        t:: platform transcript.
        twice:: Twice new.
        t show: 'who: ', twice who; newLine.
        t show: 'chain: ', twice chain; newLine.
        t show: 'lower Marker level reads markerTag as: ', twice belowSees; newLine.
        t show: 'Base slots: ', twice baseSlots; newLine.
        t show: 'Middle slot: ', twice middleSlotValue; newLine.
        t show: 'Twice slot: ', twice twiceSlotValue; newLine.
    )
) : ()
